{"games":[{"slug":"apex-legends","name":"Apex Legends","description":"A free-to-play hero battle royale set in the Outlands, a fringe region of the Titanfall universe, about 20 years after the Frontier War. The Mercenary Syndicate stages the Apex Games, a televised bloodsport, and each Legend has a backstory tied to corporate wars, simulacra, and travel between realities.","calendar":"The lore uses plain Gregorian years (CE) in the 2100s-2700s of the Titanfall universe; seasons 0-7 fall in 2733, 8-15 in 2734 and 16 onward in 2735.","events":122,"entities":121,"relationships":191,"timelines":[{"name":"The Outlands (Apex Games reality)","kind":"canon","color":"#d9c9a3","events":112},{"name":"Alter's Dying Worlds","kind":"alternate","color":"#6f8fe0","events":3},{"name":"IMC-Victory Dimension (Wraith's home reality)","kind":"alternate","color":"#d9573f","events":3},{"name":"Shadowfall Dimension (the dark Kings Canyon)","kind":"alternate","color":"#e3b23c","events":4}]},{"slug":"league-of-legends","name":"League of Legends","description":"League of Legends is set on Runeterra, a world of rival nations such as Demacia, Noxus, Ionia, Shurima and Piltover and Zaun, shaped by ancient wars between god-warriors, the Darkin, the Void and the cursed Shadow Isles. Riot Games tells the canon (Runeterra Prime) through champion biographies, stories and events, and it also runs alternate skin universes such as K/DA and Star Guardian and the Arcane TV continuity.","calendar":"Canon dates use the Noxian calendar, counted from the founding of Noxus (year 0); fans and the wiki write years before it as BN (Before Noxus) and after it as AN (After Noxus), and the exact length of a Noxian year is unknown.","events":87,"entities":180,"relationships":216,"timelines":[{"name":"Runeterra Prime (canon)","kind":"canon","color":"#d9c9a3","events":64},{"name":"Arcane (TV series)","kind":"alternate","color":"#6f8fe0","events":14},{"name":"K/DA","kind":"au","color":"#d9573f","events":5},{"name":"Star Guardian","kind":"au","color":"#e3b23c","events":4}]},{"slug":"marvel-rivals","name":"Marvel Rivals","description":"Marvel Rivals is a free-to-play team-based hero shooter by NetEase Games, released on 6 December 2024. Its story starts when Doctor Doom and Doom 2099 trigger the Timestream Entanglement, which breaks the multiverse into Chronoverses and throws heroes from different realities together. Each season adds a new story arc told through Gallery Cards, Hero Stories, events and map descriptions.","calendar":"There is no shared in-universe calendar: the Present and Collapsed timelines are set in the present day (mid-2020s) and the 2099 Timeline in 2099, so lore is labeled by the game season that told it, and sort_key places every event on one present-day axis (Timestream Entanglement = 2025.0, about 0.1 per season), with older backstory keyed to approximate years.","events":63,"entities":130,"relationships":143,"timelines":[{"name":"Present Timeline","kind":"canon","color":"#d9c9a3","events":25},{"name":"2099 Timeline","kind":"alternate","color":"#6f8fe0","events":13},{"name":"Collapsed Timeline","kind":"alternate","color":"#d9573f","events":10},{"name":"Jeff's Timeline","kind":"alternate","color":"#e3b23c","events":0},{"name":"Marvel Zombies Timeline","kind":"au","color":"#3fa39b","events":0},{"name":"Mosaic Timeline","kind":"alternate","color":"#c4467f","events":6},{"name":"Path to Doomsday Timeline","kind":"au","color":"#93b36b","events":0},{"name":"Realms Beyond the Chronoverses","kind":"alternate","color":"#9a74e0","events":9},{"name":"Venom's Timeline","kind":"alternate","color":"#b0805a","events":0},{"name":"Watercolor Timeline","kind":"alternate","color":"#7275cc","events":0}]}],"knots":{"apex-legends":[{"timeline":"The Outlands (Apex Games reality)","importance":2},{"timeline":"The Outlands (Apex Games reality)","importance":3},{"timeline":"The Outlands (Apex Games reality)","importance":3},{"timeline":"The Outlands (Apex Games reality)","importance":